    {
      "id": "claim_9296bbf7c760460dbf804862f400f1dc",
      "statement": "celld keeps a per-process compiled-bytecode cache of the ~23k lines of prelude and harness; the first isolate compiles eagerly and publishes the cache and every later isolate consumes it, so a fresh cell wake pays only execution, not compilation.",
